{
  "name": "control",
  "description": "A document that carries a Control Center control. The control is an extra, never a mode: the document still draws its one circular shape from its one text layer, and `control` sits beside `tapAction` as an optional top-level key. Kind toggle with a `toggleEntity` action stays a toggle, so the state is read: `light.kitchen` is `on`, which is one of the truthy words, so the control draws `symbol` rather than `symbolOff`. The tint comes from the band table read against the value line (42 falls in the up-to-50 band, so orange beats the flat `tintColorHex`). The compiler walks the control's title, value line, state and status the way it walks a layer, with no shape gate, so `expectedCompiled` lists the label and brightness entities beside the lamp. The action is not a reading and stays out, the same as `tapAction`.",
